cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, and cite the projects it adapts."
title: pi-sandbox-runtime
authors:
  - alias: jennymaeleidig
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-22"
license: CC0-1.0
url: "https://github.com/jennymaeleidig/pi-sandbox-runtime"
abstract: >-
  A personal pi-package that fences shell commands with the OS through
  @anthropic-ai/sandbox-runtime, and judges every Tool call — including Tools
  contributed by other packages — against the same path policy. It replaces
  carderne/pi-sandbox, which left grep, find and ls unchecked and consulted no
  policy for extension Tools. Original code is CC0-1.0; the files named below
  carry citation blocks for the MIT code they adapt.
references:
  - type: software
    title: pi-sandbox
    version: v0.6.8
    authors:
      - family-names: Arderne
        given-names: Chris
    repository-code: "https://github.com/carderne/pi-sandbox"
    commit: 31fa5060689624467c1aeace2664ce91784522ff
    license: MIT
    notes: >-
      Source of this package's src/policy.ts (path canonicalization, glob matching) and of the
      sandboxed bash operations adapted into src/sandbox.ts (detached
      process-group kill, stdio draining on exit).
  - type: software
    title: pi-mono
    authors:
      - family-names: Zechner
        given-names: Mario
    repository-code: "https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono"
    license: MIT
    notes: >-
      Upstream of pi-sandbox's sandbox example, which src/sandbox.ts descends
      from.
  - type: software
    title: sandbox-runtime
    authors:
      - name: Anthropic
    repository-code: "https://github.com/anthropics/sandbox-runtime"
    version: "0.0.77"
    license: Apache-2.0
    notes: >-
      The dependency this package wraps, not code copied from it. Pinned at
      0.0.77; its module-level SandboxManager singleton is called through the
      shim in src/sandbox.ts.
